{"study_accession":"PRJNA940708","secondary_study_accession":"SRP425507","title":"Selective modulation of gene expression in activated normal human peripheral blood mononuclear cells by store-operated calcium entry blocker BTP2","description":"Calcium is a critical signaling molecule in many cell types including immune cells. The calcium-release activated calcium channels (CRAC) responsible for store-operated calcium entry (SOCE) in immune cells are gated by STIM family members functioning as sensors of Ca2+ store content in the endoplasmic reticulum. We investigated the effect of SOCE blocker BTP2 on human peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMC) stimulated with the mitogen phytohemagglutinin (PHA). Overall design: To investigate the effect of SOCE blocker BTP2 on human peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMC) stimulated with the mitogen phytohemagglutinin (PHA), we performed RNA sequencing (RNA-seq) to query gene expression at the whole transcriptome level and identified genes differentially expressed between PBMC activated with PHA and PBMC activated with PHA in the presence of BTP2.","pubmed":"36993646;39332042","geo_series":"","n_samples":16,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN33577525","study_accession":"PRJNA940708","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"Donor4_PBMC+PHA+BTP2","description":"Donor4_PBMC+PHA+BTP2","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM7079668","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2023-08-08","attributes":[["source_name","PBMC"],["individual","Donor4"],["cell_type","PBMC"],["treatment","PHA+BTP2"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR23694778","experiment_accession":"SRX19556966","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":45103833,"base_count":9062277319,"first_public":"2023-08-08","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM7079668: Donor4_PBMC+PHA+BTP2 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"la